{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe 18 Terraform files below contain repeated, obvious, historical, or stale comments identified by the audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776`. Shortening them must preserve IAM, monitoring, and cross-file contracts.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone comments and blank lines in the declared files. Preserve HCL attributes, heredoc values, resource names, tags, and outputs byte-for-byte. Replace migration/incident narration with the minimum current rationale needed by operators.\n\n## Scope\n- `acm.tf` — Preserve shared wildcard-certificate ownership, DNS renewal, lifecycle protections, and `auth_host.tf` ARN consumption.\n- `iam_bridge_metrics.tf` — Preserve the repo-scoped OIDC role, sole `PutMetricData` permission, namespace condition, unavoidable wildcard resource, and workflow/repo-variable dependency.\n- `iam_s2.tf` — Preserve its documentation-anchor status: no IAM resources; reuse of the S1 instance role, `/rebar/prod/*` SSM read, and Session Manager.\n- `iam_s4a.tf` — Preserve no-resource status, reused instance-role data source, and workstation token writes outside the instance role.\n- `iam_s7.tf` — Preserve Claude-only Bedrock/profile bounds, invoke/stream permissions, and both profile and underlying-model ARNs.\n- `iam.tf` — Preserve EC2/DLM role ownership, Session Manager-only shell, SSM scope, KMS-via-SSM condition, CloudWatch wildcard limitation, and repo-scoped read-only drift role.\n- `monitoring_1fa8.tf` — Preserve g2p leg boundary and cadence; match current missing-data/actions.\n- `monitoring_88ab.tf` — Preserve granular merge-change metric and intentional aggregate overlap; acknowledge current SNS actions.\n- `monitoring_9ea3.tf` — Preserve end-to-end `/mcp` 401 heartbeat, distinction from deploy alarms, cadence, and AWS description-length limit.\n- `monitoring_autodeploy.tf` — Cover all current deploy-error, review-interrupt, root-disk, gate-scratch, Docker, journald, and `/var/tmp` alarms. Preserve metric dimensions/sources, publishers, thresholds/windows, missing-data semantics, complementary distinctions, and runbook pointers. The executable 1-datapoint/2-of-4 description mismatch belongs to `curricular-ulcerous-urson`.\n- `monitoring_bridge.tf` — Preserve dimensionless hourly 0/1 metric, two-failure rule, and justified `notBreaching` exception because the heartbeat canary owns stopped runs.\n- `monitoring_eb6e.tf` — Preserve AWS `ModelId` dimensions, exact three-model coupling, guarded error-rate math, idle `notBreaching`, SNS actions, and account/region provenance.\n- `monitoring_foxterrier.tf` — Preserve distinct retire-cap and memory-abort signals, fail-safe deploy meaning, 2-of-4 window, unconditional healthy zero, and SNS actions.\n- `monitoring_s4b.tf` — Preserve `VOTER_ERROR`, sustained 3-of-5 window, dimensionless/unconditional-zero contract, breaching missing data, and SNS actions.\n- `monitoring_s5.tf` — Preserve replication-log errors, divergence complement, 2-of-3 window, unconditional zero, breaching missing data, and SNS actions.\n- `monitoring_ws7.tf` — Preserve SHA-divergence role, replication-error complement, breaching missing data, and current actions.\n- `monitoring.tf` — Preserve shared SNS sink, out-of-band email confirmation, complementary Gerrit/EC2 health, non-owning backup assertion, and distinct capacity/debris alarms; attribute `aws_region` to `variables.tf`.\n- `oidc.tf` — Preserve account-singleton ownership, API-required thumbprint, and both drift and bridge-metrics role consumers.\n\nCross-file contracts: custom metrics match only on namespace/name/dimensions; most host counters publish healthy zero so silence breaches, while bridge and traffic-only Bedrock series are documented exceptions. Every alarm retains alarm/recovery SNS actions. Bedrock IDs remain coupled to provider and Compose configuration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only standalone comments or blank lines in the 18 declared files; no HCL or heredoc value changes.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked session log authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, historical, or stale prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained.\n- [ ] Terraform format/validate, focused monitoring tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and repository lint pass at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] No missing or FAIL semantic-preservation row remains at closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only guard, Terraform checks, focused monitoring/provider tests, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788598193073657001,"uuid":"ab94841b-7ebd-467e-bcf6-bc6243289683"}